1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,710
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,774 --> 00:00:09,344
A supermarket trolley!

3
00:00:10,934 --> 00:00:13,134
Which material would you choose to make it?

4
00:00:14,704 --> 00:00:15,784
One, glass.

5
00:00:17,344 --> 00:00:18,314
Two, metal.

6
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:21,074
Three, fabric.

7
00:00:23,224 --> 00:00:24,734
Hold on to your answer!

8
00:00:27,556 --> 00:00:29,016
You against the Buddies!

9
00:00:29,296 --> 00:00:30,516
Lock in first.

10
00:00:30,786 --> 00:00:32,596
One finger for every point.

11
00:00:32,886 --> 00:00:35,306
A little mynah is hiding in this video.

12
00:00:35,586 --> 00:00:36,786
Can you spot it?

13
00:00:37,364 --> 00:00:38,664
Today you'll learn:

14
00:00:38,867 --> 00:00:40,677
Objects have purposes.

15
00:00:40,873 --> 00:00:42,813
Properties decide uses.

16
00:00:43,016 --> 00:00:44,646
Why a trolley is metal.

17
00:00:45,293 --> 00:00:46,233
Are you ready?

18
00:00:46,673 --> 00:00:47,443
Three!

19
00:00:47,823 --> 00:00:48,483
Two!

20
00:00:48,853 --> 00:00:49,503
One!

21
00:00:49,923 --> 00:00:50,643
Go!

22
00:00:51,522 --> 00:00:53,452
First: what is a trolley for?

23
00:00:53,742 --> 00:00:54,852
Look closer.

24
00:00:55,505 --> 00:00:57,115
A bag of rice goes in.

25
00:00:57,735 --> 00:00:58,645
Bottles.

26
00:00:59,315 --> 00:01:00,085
Tins.

27
00:01:00,645 --> 00:01:01,925
It is heavy now.

28
00:01:02,843 --> 00:01:04,973
A push, and it all rolls along.

29
00:01:06,693 --> 00:01:09,563
A trolley is for carrying heavy groceries.

30
00:01:10,133 --> 00:01:11,803
That is its purpose.

31
00:01:15,763 --> 00:01:16,993
Say it with me!

32
00:01:17,707 --> 00:01:19,987
Materials are used to make objects.

33
00:01:20,587 --> 00:01:23,557
Objects are things you use for different purposes.

34
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:27,470
A towel.

35
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:28,620
Scissors.

36
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:29,960
A raincoat.

37
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:31,920
Each has its own purpose.

38
00:01:33,162 --> 00:01:35,692
Round one: the question from last time!

39
00:01:35,952 --> 00:01:37,662
Glass, metal, or fabric?

40
00:01:37,952 --> 00:01:39,262
Show me your fingers!

41
00:01:42,731 --> 00:01:43,711
Locked in!

42
00:01:43,839 --> 00:01:44,449
One!

43
00:01:44,589 --> 00:01:45,409
Glass!

44
00:01:45,469 --> 00:01:47,049
I can see all my snacks!

45
00:01:47,102 --> 00:01:47,562
Three.

46
00:01:48,162 --> 00:01:51,662
My fabric bag carries heavy books, and it does not tear.

47
00:01:51,709 --> 00:01:52,489
Two!

48
00:01:52,569 --> 00:01:54,519
The trolleys here are all metal!

49
00:01:55,471 --> 00:01:56,621
Look closer.

50
00:01:57,211 --> 00:02:00,071
The metal trolley, full of heavy groceries.

51
00:02:00,596 --> 00:02:02,376
The metal bars stay straight.

52
00:02:02,946 --> 00:02:04,236
They do not bend.

53
00:02:06,342 --> 00:02:08,652
Now it rolls into the trolley bay.

54
00:02:09,252 --> 00:02:10,022
Clang!

55
00:02:10,592 --> 00:02:11,802
A hard knock.

56
00:02:15,109 --> 00:02:16,129
No crack.

57
00:02:16,749 --> 00:02:17,779
No break.

58
00:02:18,379 --> 00:02:19,659
Metal is strong.

59
00:02:23,455 --> 00:02:25,965
Glass is fragile, but metal is strong.

60
00:02:26,245 --> 00:02:29,465
A glass cup breaks easily when it is dropped, but a metal

61
00:02:29,485 --> 00:02:30,615
cup does not.

62
00:02:31,701 --> 00:02:32,411
Oops.

63
00:02:32,471 --> 00:02:33,781
Bye-bye, snacks!

64
00:02:35,216 --> 00:02:36,246
And fabric?

65
00:02:36,506 --> 00:02:38,266
Pip's bag holds the rice.

66
00:02:38,516 --> 00:02:41,156
But it folds flat: fabric is flexible.

67
00:02:41,938 --> 00:02:42,658
Oh!

68
00:02:42,938 --> 00:02:44,728
A trolley must not bend!

69
00:02:44,854 --> 00:02:46,164
The answer is two.

70
00:02:46,444 --> 00:02:47,244
Metal!

71
00:02:47,524 --> 00:02:48,554
Two fingers?

72
00:02:48,824 --> 00:02:50,034
One finger up!

73
00:02:51,263 --> 00:02:52,413
Say it with me!

74
00:02:53,127 --> 00:02:55,367
Every material has physical properties.

75
00:02:55,877 --> 00:02:59,057
The physical properties of a material allow it to be used in

76
00:02:59,077 --> 00:03:00,307
certain ways.

77
00:03:03,532 --> 00:03:05,462
So glass is a bad material!

78
00:03:05,542 --> 00:03:07,482
Never use glass for anything!

79
00:03:07,603 --> 00:03:09,163
Something is not right.

80
00:03:09,433 --> 00:03:11,613
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

81
00:03:11,893 --> 00:03:12,853
Hold on!

82
00:03:18,366 --> 00:03:19,496
Arms crossed?

83
00:03:19,766 --> 00:03:20,926
One finger up!

84
00:03:21,206 --> 00:03:23,126
Glass is not a bad material.

85
00:03:23,396 --> 00:03:24,956
It depends on the use.

86
00:03:25,306 --> 00:03:26,326
Hold on, Momo!

87
00:03:26,506 --> 00:03:28,436
The fish tank next door is glass!

88
00:03:29,308 --> 00:03:30,438
Look closer.

89
00:03:31,048 --> 00:03:33,218
A glass fish tank, full of water.

90
00:03:33,724 --> 00:03:35,704
We can see every fish clearly.

91
00:03:36,284 --> 00:03:37,914
Glass is transparent.

92
00:03:40,036 --> 00:03:41,796
The shelf under it is dry.

93
00:03:42,376 --> 00:03:44,006
No water passes through.

94
00:03:44,596 --> 00:03:46,196
Glass is waterproof.

95
00:03:46,707 --> 00:03:49,677
For a fish tank, glass is the right material!

96
00:03:53,574 --> 00:03:53,904
Oh!

97
00:03:53,924 --> 00:03:55,684
The same glass.

98
00:03:55,754 --> 00:03:57,074
A different use!

99
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,420
Be the metal!

100
00:03:58,730 --> 00:03:59,710
Shrink down.

101
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:00,920
Quietly.

102
00:04:03,202 --> 00:04:06,322
You are a metal bar, at the bottom of the trolley.

103
00:04:07,043 --> 00:04:09,193
A heavy bag of rice lands on you.

104
00:04:09,963 --> 00:04:11,273
You do not bend.

105
00:04:11,938 --> 00:04:13,128
The wheels roll.

106
00:04:13,928 --> 00:04:15,648
The floor rushes past.

107
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:17,171
Clang!

108
00:04:17,961 --> 00:04:19,081
A hard knock.

109
00:04:19,921 --> 00:04:21,121
You do not break.

110
00:04:21,961 --> 00:04:23,051
You are strong!

111
00:04:25,328 --> 00:04:26,788
Show me your score hand!

112
00:04:27,068 --> 00:04:28,458
One finger or more?

113
00:04:28,778 --> 00:04:30,138
You beat the Buddies.

114
00:04:30,408 --> 00:04:31,438
Two fingers?

115
00:04:31,718 --> 00:04:32,728
High five!

116
00:04:33,375 --> 00:04:34,695
Did you spot the mynah?

117
00:04:35,025 --> 00:04:36,815
It was on the trolley bay sign!

118
00:04:37,085 --> 00:04:38,385
Tell someone at home.

119
00:04:39,111 --> 00:04:41,311
Let's read today's key words together!

120
00:04:41,601 --> 00:04:42,361
Ready?

121
00:04:42,698 --> 00:04:43,420
Purpose.

122
00:04:44,890 --> 00:04:46,300
Physical properties.

123
00:04:48,122 --> 00:04:49,062
Well done!

124
00:04:49,959 --> 00:04:50,519
Look!

125
00:04:50,689 --> 00:04:52,619
Three water bottles in our trolley!

126
00:04:52,672 --> 00:04:53,822
One plastic.

127
00:04:54,092 --> 00:04:55,122
One glass.

128
00:04:55,442 --> 00:04:56,362
One metal.

129
00:04:56,652 --> 00:04:58,882
The same object, three materials!

130
00:04:59,152 --> 00:05:00,832
Which one is right for school?

131
00:05:00,885 --> 00:05:02,475
Find out in Part Two!

132
00:05:03,835 --> 00:05:04,936
Say it with us!

133
00:05:05,736 --> 00:05:06,486
Ready?

134
00:05:06,609 --> 00:05:07,269
One!

135
00:05:07,609 --> 00:05:08,309
two!

136
00:05:08,614 --> 00:05:09,789
Now you know!
